Recommends: homelab-agent
Description: Fleet TLS certificate issuance (DNS-01) and publication
 Owns certificate issuance for the whole fleet from ONE dedicated host, so
 renewal no longer depends on which internet-facing edge node happens to be
 powered on -- the problem with per-edge certbot under a manual, one-node-at-a-
 time edge model, where a standby holds no ACME account and silently cannot
 renew anything.
 .
 Solves ACME challenges over DNS-01 through homelab-api's narrow, system_agent-
 gated _acme-challenge endpoint, so this host needs no inbound :80/:443 (it is
 never public-facing) and holds no credential capable of editing arbitrary DNS.
 .
 Each issued certificate is envelope-encrypted here, under a key-encryption-key
 held only in this host's config, and published to the shared certificate store
 in homelab-api. The API therefore stores and serves ciphertext and can never
 hand out a usable private key; only a consumer holding the same KEK can
 decrypt. Consumers pull with homelab-certsync.
